{"name":"Hazelnut Turkish Delight","hex":"#fce974","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hazelnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit of the hazel, especially of species Corylus avellana, which is grown commercially.","A light tan color inspired by the color of hazelnut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazelnut"},{"term":"delight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Joy; pleasure.","Something that gives great joy or pleasure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give delight to; to affect with great pleasure; to please highly.","To have or take great pleasure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turkish delight","blocks":[{"text":"Turkish delight, lokum or loqum is a family of confections based on a gel of starch and sugar. Premium varieties consist largely of chopped dates, pistachios, hazelnuts or walnuts bound by the gel; traditional varieties are often flavored with rosewater, mastic gum, bergamot orange, or lemon. Other common flavors include cinnamon and mint. The confection is often packaged in small cubes dusted with icing sugar, copra, or powdered cream of tartar to prevent clinging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/TurkishDelightDisplay.jpg/330px-TurkishDelightDisplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkish_delight","wikidata":"Q182339"},{"title":"Hazelnut","blocks":[{"text":"The hazelnut is the fruit of the hazel tree and therefore includes any of the nuts deriving from species of the genus Corylus, especially the nuts of the species Corylus avellana. They are also known as cobnuts or filberts according to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg/330px-Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org